Title: How do I create a Java string from the contents of a file?.
Body: <p>I've been using the idiom below for some time now. And it seems to be the most wide-spread, at least on the sites I've visited.</p>
<p>Is there a better/different way to read a file into a string in Java?</p>
<pre><code>private String readFile(String file) throws IOException {
    BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader (file));
    String line = null;
    StringBuilder stringBuilder = new StringBuilder();
    String ls = System.getProperty(&quot;line.separator&quot;);

    try {
        while((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            stringBuilder.append(line);
            stringBuilder.append(ls);
        }

        return stringBuilder.toString();
    } finally {
        reader.close();
    }
}
</code></pre>

